/*
  ========================================================================================
  Project: Offline Acoustic Detection of Hidden Insect Infestation in Stored Grains
  Target:  ARIES Vega V2.0 (CDAC RISC-V THEJAS Core)
  IDE:     Arduino IDE 2.3.x / ARIES Vega Board Package (vega:riscv:aries_v2)
  ========================================================================================

  HARDWARE ASSIGNMENTS:
    - A0 = Lower Stainless-Steel Probe + Piezo AFE (P1)
    - A1 = Upper Stainless-Steel Probe + Piezo AFE (P2)
    - A2 = MAX4466 Microphone AFE (Ambient Acoustic Reference)
    - GPIO11 = Green LED (NORMAL)
    - GPIO12 = Yellow LED (INSECT ACTIVITY)
    - GPIO13 = Red LED (EXTERNAL DISTURBANCE)
    - GPIO14 = Active 5V Buzzer via 2N2222A Transistor Driver
    - GPIO15 = Push Button for Mute / Reset (INPUT_PULLUP)
    - I2C (SCL/SDA) = 0.96" SSD1306 OLED Display (Address 0x3C)

  KEY DESIGN & ARIES VEGA V2 COMPATIBILITY HIGHLIGHTS:
    1. TwoWire Wire(0) explicitly instantiated:
       In the ARIES Vega core library, TwoWire Wire(0) is commented out in Wire.cpp,
       requiring user code to instantiate the bus object directly.
    2. 16-byte I2C FIFO Buffer Safety:
       The SSD1306 driver sends display data strictly in 8-byte chunks (+1 command byte
       = 9 bytes total per transmission) to avoid hardware FIFO overflow.
    3. Completely Self-Contained:
       No external OLED or FFT libraries required; no AVR-only functions (dtostrf, ltoa);
       no ESP32-only calls. Runs deterministically on RISC-V.
    4. Windowed DSP Pipeline:
       - Synchronous 128-point acquisition of P1, P2, and MIC.
       - Independent DC baseline calibration and quiet noise floor tracking.
       - Hann windowing + fast in-place Radix-2 FFT.
       - 15 time-domain, spectral, and temporal event features calculated per window.
    5. Four-Scenario Real Hardware Discrimination:
       - Normal grain: Probes and mic quiet, Green LED ON, Buzzer OFF.
       - Real insect activity: Localized small/medium mechanical bursts (sensitive to
         ~170 count excursions on lower probe), high probe-to-mic ratio, repeated
         transient clicks confirming across multiple windows.
       - Container knock / tap / handling: High-crest synchronized dual-probe shock +
         loud microphone impulse -> classified as EXTERNAL DISTURBANCE, never INSECT.
       - Environmental noise / speech / clapping: Loud microphone alone without probe
         vibrations is rejected and stays NORMAL.
  ========================================================================================
*/

